<http://data.silknow.org/object/d6a7341e-0061-33d1-8b53-c83239b9326b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Piece of border, probably from table cover pale neutral brown linen crossed, horizontally, by a band of embroidery between two narrower bands, with one band across the end. Design: stylized plant forms, stags, unicorns, dogs and small birds worked with red silk and pale brown linen thread in satin stitch, and Holbein or double-running stitich, the background, drawn-work with loop filling. Gauze weave fring woven with pale brown, and pinkish red linen sewed across bottom. Frail, torn."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6a7341e-0061-33d1-8b53-c83239b9326b> .

